This penetration testing report details the authorized, educational security assessment of the Mediroza General Hospital web application. Conducted as part of Week 4 of the NetworkWalks Penetration Testing Internship, the engagement was performed with full permission and within a controlled, educational environment.
The assessment revealed that the hospital's web application is hosted on a shared environment with certain misconfigurations and that the application’s login mechanisms could be tested for username enumeration vulnerabilities.
No actual exploitation or unauthorized access was conducted beyond simulation, and all activities were carried out under an approved, ethical learning framework.
